[[SECTION]]
UID: L1-VP
TITLE: Value proposition

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
### Executive summary

*Include this only if there are four or more customer segments.* Below that
threshold it repeats the specifications that follow.

TBD - A visual overview such as a Value Proposition Canvas, plus one or two
paragraphs naming each segment and the value it receives.
<<<

[VALUE_PROPOSITION]
UID: VP-01
CUSTOMER_SEGMENT: TBD
SEGMENT_SIZE: TBD
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: For TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - The value this segment receives. Benefits and outcomes, never features.
<<<
SEGMENT_CHARACTERISTICS: >>>
TBD - Who this segment is and what matters about them for design purposes.
<<<
VALUE_DELIVERED: >>>
TBD - Three to seven key benefits:

- What problems does the solution solve for them?
- What improvements will they experience?
- What new capabilities do they gain?
<<<
PAINS_ADDRESSED: >>>
TBD - The specific frustrations this removes.
<<<
CURRENT_ALTERNATIVES: >>>
TBD - *Optional, for competitive contexts.* How this segment meets the need
today without the solution. Be concrete: "standing in line for 20-30 minutes",
"manual aggregation using paper forms and phone calls".
<<<
WHY_BETTER: >>>
TBD - *Optional.* Why the proposed solution beats those alternatives. Time
savings, convenience, quality, cost, or capabilities not previously available.
Quantify where possible.
<<<
