[[SECTION]]
UID: L1-VCA
TITLE: Value creation architecture

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
### Executive summary

TBD - One or two paragraphs on the overall value creation structure: who the
main stakeholder groups are, what role the digital elements play, and how value
flows through the architecture.

Include a diagram showing customers who receive value, the internal and external
organisations involved, the digital elements that enable value creation, and the
key relationships between them.

```mermaid
graph LR
  CUST["VCA-01 TBD customer"]
  ORG["VCA-02 TBD organisation"]
  DIG["VCA-03 TBD digital element"]
  CUST --> DIG
  DIG --> ORG
```
<<<

[VALUE_CREATION_ELEMENT]
UID: VCA-01
ELEMENT_TYPE: Digital-element
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - This element and its role in value creation, in two or three sentences.

For a **customer**: who they are and what they want to achieve.
For an **organisation**: what they do and what they are responsible for.
For a **digital element**: what capability it provides.

*Granularity for digital elements:* for a simple solution, the whole technical
system can be one digital element ("The Platform"). Break it down only where the
distinction matters to business stakeholders. L2 provides the technical
decomposition into software elements regardless of how many digital elements are
named here.
<<<
ROLE_IN_VALUE_CREATION: >>>
TBD - What this element does to create or deliver value. For customers, how they
interact and what they receive; for organisations, what activities they perform;
for digital elements, what functionality they enable.
<<<
INTERACTS_WITH: >>>
TBD - Other value creation elements this one interacts with, as inline links:
[LINK: VCA-02].

These are peer relationships rather than hierarchy, so they are recorded as
links rather than as relations - a lateral relation modelled as Parent breaks
the traceability graph.
<<<
VALUE_FLOW: >>>
TBD - For a customer, the value received (reference the VP). For an organisation
or digital element, the value it provides or enables.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: VP-01
  ROLE: Realises

