[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: L1-BQR
TITLE: Quality requirements

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Business-level quality expectations that must be met for the solution to be
considered successful. Stated from the stakeholder perspective, in business
categories rather than technical quality attributes - those appear at L2 as SQR
items refining these.
<<<

[BUSINESS_QUALITY_REQUIREMENT]
UID: BQR-01
QUALITY_CATEGORY: Customer-satisfaction
OBLIGATION: shall
PRIORITY: Must
STATUS: Draft
VERIFICATION: Review
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - What aspect of business quality is specified and why it matters to
stakeholders. Two or three sentences.

Categories: `Business-performance` for revenue, cost, efficiency and
productivity; `Customer-satisfaction` for satisfaction, retention and adoption;
`Service-quality` for availability, reliability and accuracy as the business
sees them; `Operational-excellence` for process quality and resource
utilisation; `Compliance` for regulatory and policy requirements;
`Sustainability` for environmental impact and long-term viability.
<<<
APPLIES_TO: >>>
TBD - Which business elements this primarily affects: [LINK: BP-01],
[LINK: VP-01], [LINK: VCA-01], or the overall business solution.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA: >>>
TBD - Clear, testable, verifiable from a business perspective.

**Quantitative** where metrics, satisfaction, performance, adoption or service
levels can be measured - include the number:
- "Satisfaction score >= 85% in quarterly surveys"
- "Available during all operating hours, 06:00-20:00 weekdays"

**Qualitative** where assessment is subjective, compliance is binary, or the
requirement is a capability - use a clear pass/fail condition:
- "Students can complete ordering without staff assistance"
- "All allergens clearly communicated to customers"
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
TBD - *Optional.*
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BG-01
  ROLE: Satisfies

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: L1-BC
TITLE: Constraints

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Non-negotiable requirements limiting design and implementation choices. They
come from outside - laws, regulations, budgets, timelines, organisational
policy - and are not trade-offs to be balanced.
<<<

[BUSINESS_CONSTRAINT]
UID: BC-01
CONSTRAINT_CATEGORY: Legal-regulatory
STATUS: Draft
SOURCE: TBD
TITLE: TBD
STATEMENT: >>>
TBD - What the constraint requires or restricts, and why it exists from a
business perspective. Two or three sentences.

Categories: `Legal-regulatory` for laws, regulations and compliance;
`Business` for budget limits, timelines and organisational policy;
`Organisational` for existing processes, structures or capabilities that must be
accommodated; `Market` for competitive pressure, customer expectations and
industry norms; `Resource` for staff, skills and infrastructure limitations.
<<<
APPLIES_TO: >>>
TBD - Which business elements are affected: [LINK: BP-01], [LINK: VP-01],
[LINK: VCA-01], or the overall business solution.
<<<
ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA: >>>
TBD - What demonstrates compliance, from a business perspective.

**Quantitative** where the constraint has amounts, dates or limits:
- "Total budget not to exceed 150,000"
- "Operational by the start of the autumn term"
- "Personal data retained for a maximum of 24 months"

**Qualitative** where compliance is binary or an approach is mandated:
- "Complies with GDPR requirements for personal data handling"
- "Uses the existing university authentication system; no new login"
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
TBD - *Optional.*
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BRC-01
